<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="skill">choir-focus-gems</ansi> (jewelcrafting recipe)

A matched ring of cut gems, each faceted to the same angle as its
neighbors, tuned until set together they hold a single chord rather than
six separate notes. Strung or set in sequence, the gems focus what
passes through them into one clean line of sound, refusing to let the
chord fray at the edges. Jewelers tune them by ear, not by eye.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Crafting ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="yellow">Skill:</ansi>       jewelcrafting (minimum 50)
  <ansi fg="yellow">Station:</ansi>     jeweler_bench
  <ansi fg="yellow">Ingredients:</ansi> Raw Gem (x2), Gem Dust (x1), Gold Wire (x1)

